WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.109 --> 00:00:00.942
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:00:00.942 --> 00:00:04.191
- H! Nice to meet you
guys, nice to meet you!

00:00:04.191 --> 00:00:05.960
I love having the whole family here.

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:07.402
(audience cheering)

00:00:07.402 --> 00:00:08.403
Oh my gosh.

00:00:08.403 --> 00:00:11.010
So, Charli you led the way with dancing.

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:12.340
So have you always been a dancer?

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:13.250
- Yes, I've been-

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:14.280
- Oh my God, I didn't notice

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.290
you had freckles til just now.

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:17.780
Y'all are adorable, those freckles.

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:18.640
Sorry, keep going.

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:20.630
- No, I've been taking dance classes

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:23.040
since I was three and competing
since I was five years old

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:24.660
so quite some time, yeah.

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:26.250
- [Kelly] It's so fun though, dancing.

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:27.083
- Oh, yeah.

00:00:27.083 --> 00:00:28.210
- Oh my gosh, and is it like,

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:30.410
I find that it like
helps me relieve stress.

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:31.778
- [Charli] Oh, a hundred percent.

00:00:31.778 --> 00:00:32.611
- I will literally dance alone in my room

00:00:32.611 --> 00:00:33.950
after I put my kids to bed.

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:35.550
I live a very different life from you.

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:37.720
And I will put on music
and literally just dance

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:39.270
by myself to make myself feel better.

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:40.500
- It's so fun.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:41.560
- [Kelly] Yes, yes.

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:43.370
Okay, so what did you think, you know,

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:45.920
or I guess, what did think
it was about Charli's videos

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:47.310
that, you know, was so
appealing to people?

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:49.104
Why do you think people
started freaking out?

00:00:49.104 --> 00:00:51.430
- I think just the fact that she

00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:55.510
let people into a normal
teenager's life in her bedroom.

00:00:55.510 --> 00:00:56.343
I say it all the time,

00:00:56.343 --> 00:00:57.807
one of the first things we would say is,

00:00:57.807 --> 00:01:00.160
"Don't you wanna make your
bed or clean up a little bit?"

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:02.927
And she's just like "No dad,
this is what everybody wants."

00:01:02.927 --> 00:01:04.604
- Authentic, be authentic.

00:01:04.604 --> 00:01:05.437
(mom laughing)

00:01:05.437 --> 00:01:07.402
- Yeah, oh hey, that's very
authentic for a teenager.

00:01:07.402 --> 00:01:09.560
Well Dixie, you sing and dance as well,

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:10.470
very talented family,

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:12.620
but I heard that you have a hidden talent,

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:14.140
so, what is that?

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:15.300
- My hidden talent is that I can

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:17.087
play the piano with my toes.

00:01:17.087 --> 00:01:18.420
- What?

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:21.720
- So, growing up I spent a
lot of time, like, by myself.

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:23.720
Charli didn't love playing
with me when we were kids.

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:24.780
So, I-

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:26.740
- That happens when you're
the younger sister by the way.

00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:28.580
Lisa, you hear me out there, Lisa Beth?

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:30.710
Yeah, I know you didn't
want to play with me.

00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:32.440
- So, I played the violin,

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:35.100
and I wanted to play the
piano at the same time.

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:38.470
So, I just learned how to
do both at the same time.

00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:40.450
- Wait, that is the weirdest thing I ever,

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:42.530
most people can't even like
play with their fingers

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:43.540
let alone their toes.

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:44.373
- Yeah.

00:01:44.373 --> 00:01:45.430
- And by weird, I mean really cool.

00:01:45.430 --> 00:01:46.984
- I had a lot of free time as a kid.

00:01:46.984 --> 00:01:48.910
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:48.910 --> 00:01:50.530
- Oh my God, I love you.

00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:53.860
Okay, so Charli you recently
had your wisdom teeth

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:56.090
pulled so here you are
in the car afterward,

00:01:56.090 --> 00:01:57.020
I love these videos.

00:01:57.020 --> 00:01:58.620
- Is it okay?

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:00.660
- Yeah, it's cause they put medicine.

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:01.493
- Oh okay

00:02:01.493 --> 00:02:02.996
- Yeah, yeah it'll come back.

00:02:02.996 --> 00:02:03.829
(Charli crying out)

00:02:03.829 --> 00:02:05.119
Where is she?

00:02:05.119 --> 00:02:06.549
She might be working.

00:02:06.549 --> 00:02:07.998
It's all right.

00:02:07.998 --> 00:02:10.898
- It's okay, I love you Dixie.

00:02:10.898 --> 00:02:14.613
- I love your ending, I love people.

00:02:14.613 --> 00:02:16.150
It's the weirdest thing how much

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:17.500
I love watching people coming out of

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:18.850
the dentist office in these videos.

00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:20.380
Um, do you remember any of that?

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:23.487
- I remember my whole face
was really, really numb.

00:02:23.487 --> 00:02:24.540
- Oh.

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:27.360
- Um, it was definite,
looking back at the videos,

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:28.830
I think I had a really good reaction.

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:32.100
I did not know what to expect
at all, especially after.

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:33.640
- Wait, oh yeah that's
right, that's right.

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:35.870
We actually, we didn't leave Dixie out.

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:37.570
We actually have hers as well.

00:02:37.570 --> 00:02:38.670
We want to be fair here.

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:39.984
Let's play Dixie's.

00:02:39.984 --> 00:02:40.944
(Kelly chuckling)

00:02:40.944 --> 00:02:43.738
- Mom. Literally I'm fine.

00:02:43.738 --> 00:02:45.827
Let me eat anything.

00:02:45.827 --> 00:02:46.668
- [Heidi] It's not happening.

00:02:46.668 --> 00:02:47.501
- Why?

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:49.548
- Because.

00:02:49.548 --> 00:02:52.637
- Please. I just want a burger.

00:02:52.637 --> 00:02:53.470
- [Heidi] I'm not-

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:57.362
(Kelly laughing and crowd clapping)

00:02:57.362 --> 00:02:59.300
- Literally, I'm fine.

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:00.752
Um, it's amazing, so wait,

00:03:00.752 --> 00:03:02.540
you really wanted a burger though?

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:05.330
- Yeah, I hated the fact that my mom

00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:07.620
was like, we can have
ice cream or anything.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:08.710
I just wanted a burger.

00:03:08.710 --> 00:03:10.110
I don't remember that at all.

00:03:10.110 --> 00:03:11.990
I don't remember coming
out of the doctor's office.

00:03:11.990 --> 00:03:13.050
They just showed me the video later.

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:14.826
I'm like, I don't even
like burgers that much.

00:03:14.826 --> 00:03:15.659
(audience laughing)

00:03:15.659 --> 00:03:16.492
I don't know what was going on.

00:03:16.492 --> 00:03:17.810
- Or do you? Like deep
down, subconsciously.

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:18.994
- I mean I guess.

00:03:18.994 --> 00:03:21.330
That wass what I was
craving. I don't know.

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:23.330
- It's amazing what happens sometimes

00:03:23.330 --> 00:03:24.230
when you leave the dentist.

00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:28.310
Um, well um, trust me I
went on a shopping spree

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:30.155
and had no idea what I was doing it.

00:03:30.155 --> 00:03:31.390
It was very not safe.

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:34.110
Um, but Marc and Heidi, so
between Charli and Dixie

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:35.688
who is more dramatic?

00:03:35.688 --> 00:03:36.744
- Charli.

00:03:36.744 --> 00:03:38.376
- Hands, hands down.

00:03:38.376 --> 00:03:39.455
- Oh! There was no hesitation.

00:03:39.455 --> 00:03:41.246
(Kelly laughing)

00:03:41.246 --> 00:03:42.980
- I wouldn't disagree.

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:44.040
- So, Charli your dad tried

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:46.180
to teach you to drive. How'd that go?

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:48.890
- So, in our old house before we

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:50.440
moved to the one we are in now.

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:52.650
Our driveway was really,
really complicated,

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:54.960
and it was really tight and of course the

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:57.080
first time I wanted to
really take initiative

00:03:57.080 --> 00:03:59.304
and drive the car was in to that driveway.

00:03:59.304 --> 00:04:00.250
- Oh.

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:01.610
- And last minute I freaked out,

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:03.050
and I forgot which one was the gas

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:04.113
and which one was the brake.

00:04:04.113 --> 00:04:04.946
(audience laughing)

00:04:04.946 --> 00:04:06.200
- Did you run into the garage?

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:07.033
- I didn't.

00:04:07.033 --> 00:04:10.167
I actually ran into the
sidewalk of my neighbors yard.

00:04:10.167 --> 00:04:12.150
- Okay, you didn't the house, oh.

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:13.400
- But I didn't hit anything.

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:14.550
- [Kelly] But it wasn't like, your lawn.

00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:15.530
- Mm, no.

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:17.901
- That was a good day for that one,

00:04:17.901 --> 00:04:19.013
at least you didn't hit the house.

00:04:19.013 --> 00:04:20.077
- Right?

00:04:20.077 --> 00:04:21.092
- I remember my brother, when I was little

00:04:21.092 --> 00:04:22.430
he like did the wrong pedal and went into

00:04:22.430 --> 00:04:25.220
the garage with the door
closed. Um, so how do

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:27.660
how do you think driving lessons went?

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:29.300
- I feel bad because I wanted it

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:33.950
to be that experience
that dads and kids have

00:04:33.950 --> 00:04:36.760
when you take your daughter
out and I did a dad

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:38.660
move and got and I just grabbed the wheel

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:40.590
and went like that and I
got her really nervous so.

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:43.060
- Um, I don't think I'm ever
gonna do that with my kids.

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:44.660
I will let somebody else do that.

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:45.950
It would drive me nuts.

00:04:45.950 --> 00:04:47.460
I think yeah, I know this.

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:49.020
I'm not gonna do that to my children.

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:51.220
Um, but putting videos online and being

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:53.090
as popular as you are, um, and as popular

00:04:53.090 --> 00:04:54.530
as your videos are.

00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:55.710
Can sometimes get blow back.

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:56.880
I've been in the public eye for 20 years.

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:58.760
You can get some nasty people out there.

00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:00.070
I advise you to never read it.

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:01.280
Don't read the good or the bad.

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:02.316
- Yeah.

00:05:02.316 --> 00:05:03.149
- Because if you read the good, your ego

00:05:03.149 --> 00:05:05.730
explodes and you become
just an unlikable human.

00:05:05.730 --> 00:05:07.880
And then if you read
the bad, then you wanna

00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:09.611
crawl in a hole and die
cause people are so mean.

00:05:09.611 --> 00:05:10.444
- Yeah.

00:05:10.444 --> 00:05:11.950
- So, it's really not a
good, it's not a way to win,

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:13.520
but what is your experience from it?

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:15.340
Cause y'all are of an
age where social media

00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:17.440
is just so different than it was for us.

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:19.150
We didn't have this kind of pressure.

00:05:19.150 --> 00:05:20.170
How do you handle it?

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:21.970
- I feel like we're doing a lot better

00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:25.860
of a job now at, not really
reading it because obviously

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:27.350
you want to read all the great stuff

00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:28.790
but with that comes the negative.

00:05:28.790 --> 00:05:32.380
So it's just easier to kind
of not look at it and then

00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:34.360
engage with only the positive.

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:36.250
I used to engage with a
lot of the negative and

00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:38.310
it would draw people's attention to it

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:40.500
and now I just appreciate the people that

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:42.696
appreciate me and I think that's
the best way to handle it.

00:05:42.696 --> 00:05:43.529
(audience clapping)

00:05:43.529 --> 00:05:45.003
- Yeah, absolutely!

00:05:45.003 --> 00:05:46.832
And just people can be mean.

00:05:46.832 --> 00:05:49.042
People can be mean, they
just wanna say mean things

00:05:49.042 --> 00:05:51.110
cause their so unhappy and it's like worry

00:05:51.110 --> 00:05:52.390
about yourselves, stay in your lane,

00:05:52.390 --> 00:05:53.580
get on your own front porch.

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:55.510
Um, but I don't know I
always say, don't look at it.

00:05:55.510 --> 00:05:56.630
I still say don't look at it.

00:05:56.630 --> 00:05:57.468
(crowd laughing)

00:05:57.468 --> 00:05:59.900
But anyway, but why,
why did you want to do

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:02.630
the docuseries, like why were
y'all interested in this?

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:04.330
- I think for the reason that when

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:09.330
the kids got on social media
everybody had a preconceived

00:06:09.330 --> 00:06:11.230
notion of who we are and
we're like well if we're

00:06:11.230 --> 00:06:15.760
going to be this popular and
they're putting ourselves

00:06:15.760 --> 00:06:17.790
out there we might as well
let people into our lives

00:06:17.790 --> 00:06:21.140
and then if they don't like
us, then they don't like who

00:06:21.140 --> 00:06:24.720
us we really are not just
a 15 second video of us.

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:25.960
- Absolutely.

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:28.550
Um, so we've seen you guys dance a ton.

00:06:28.550 --> 00:06:30.100
I love dancing.

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:31.890
Um, we should see what your parents

00:06:31.890 --> 00:06:33.361
can do um is what I'm saying.

00:06:33.361 --> 00:06:34.800
(audience cheering)

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:36.065
- I love that.

00:06:36.065 --> 00:06:39.080
- We have, we have seen your moves.

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:41.878
But we have not seen
where they have come from.

00:06:41.878 --> 00:06:42.711
(Heidi laughing)

00:06:42.711 --> 00:06:43.544
Okay, well why don't y'all get up.

00:06:43.544 --> 00:06:45.970
Let's see y'all's moves, let's see it.

00:06:45.970 --> 00:06:47.012
Come on, come on

00:06:47.012 --> 00:06:47.845
- Right up here?

00:06:47.845 --> 00:06:49.507
- You can do it! You can do it!

00:06:49.507 --> 00:06:50.737
(audience cheering)

00:06:50.737 --> 00:06:51.993
I'm gonna get up and dance.

00:06:51.993 --> 00:06:53.417
(upbeat music starts playing)

00:06:53.417 --> 00:06:57.250
(clapping and Kelly cheering)

00:07:01.687 --> 00:07:04.687
Oh my God, your parents are so cute.

00:07:06.222 --> 00:07:07.072
They are so cute!

